## Strategy Components

### Volatility Analysis
- VIX calculation implementation based on CBOE methodology
- Volatility term structure analysis
- Mean reversion signals based on VIX levels
- Volatility regime detection

### Risk Management Rules
1. Position Sizing
   - Scale position size inversely with VIX
   - Maximum position size at low volatility: 10%
   - Reduced position size in high volatility regimes

2. Volatility-Based Filters
   - No entries when VIX > historical 75th percentile
   - Reduced position size when VIX trending up
   - Exit positions on volatility spikes

3. Mean Reversion Parameters
   - Entry when price deviates > 2 standard deviations
   - Exit when price reverts to mean
   - Adjust thresholds based on volatility regime

## Development Guidelines
- Implement proper unit tests for VIX calculation
- Document all risk parameters and their rationale
- Log all volatility regime changes
- Track mean reversion statistics